# SAM overlay — Cognito + JWT authorizer (Fase 4)

Use este arquivo como referência para estender [`template.yaml`](template.yaml) quando migrar auth para Cognito.

Baseado em [re:Money security](https://dev.to/vsenger/goodbye-localhost-hello-aws-adding-security-to-remoney-2063).

## Pré-requisitos

1. Google OAuth Client ID/Secret (opcional, para login Google)
2. Callback URL: `https://<ApiId>.execute-api.<region>.amazonaws.com/auth/callback`
3. `auth.js` + rota `/auth/callback` já implementados no Quarkus

## Recursos a adicionar ao template.yaml

```yaml
Parameters:
  GoogleClientId:
    Type: String
    Default: ""
  GoogleClientSecret:
    Type: String
    NoEcho: true
    Default: ""

Conditions:
  UseGoogleAuth: !Not [!Equals [!Ref GoogleClientId, ""]]

Resources:
  ChecklistUserPool:
    Type: AWS::Cognito::UserPool
    Properties:
      UserPoolName: checklist-boteco-users
      AutoVerifiedAttributes: [email]

  ChecklistUserPoolDomain:
    Type: AWS::Cognito::UserPoolDomain
    Properties:
      Domain: checklist-boteco-auth-UNIQUE
      UserPoolId: !Ref ChecklistUserPool

  ChecklistUserPoolClient:
    Type: AWS::Cognito::UserPoolClient
    Properties:
      ClientName: checklist-web
      UserPoolId: !Ref ChecklistUserPool
      GenerateSecret: false
      AllowedOAuthFlows: [implicit]
      AllowedOAuthScopes: [openid, email, profile]
      AllowedOAuthFlowsUserPoolClient: true
      CallbackURLs:
        - https://YOUR-API.execute-api.us-east-1.amazonaws.com/auth/callback
      LogoutURLs:
        - https://YOUR-API.execute-api.us-east-1.amazonaws.com/

  ChecklistHttpApi:
    Type: AWS::Serverless::HttpApi
    Properties:
      Auth:
        DefaultAuthorizer: CognitoAuthorizer
        Authorizers:
          CognitoAuthorizer:
            IdentitySource: "$request.header.Authorization"
            JwtConfiguration:
              issuer: !Sub https://cognito-idp.${AWS::Region}.amazonaws.com/${ChecklistUserPool}
              audience: [!Ref ChecklistUserPoolClient]
```

## Rotas

| Rota | Auth gateway | Auth app |
|------|--------------|----------|
| `/`, `/assets/*`, `/auth/callback` | Pública | Callback sem guard |
| `/api/*` | JWT Cognito | AdminGuard valida claims |

## Próximos passos código

1. `admin.js`: login redirect para hosted UI Cognito quando `checklist.auth.mode=cognito`
2. Mapear claims Cognito → `PermissionLevel` / `FeaturePermissions`
3. App Android: Hosted UI ou SRP contra User Pool
4. Desativar `TokenService` HMAC em `%prod` após cutover

## Dev local

Manter auth HMAC + 2FA em `%dev`. Cognito só em stack AWS com parâmetros configurados.
